{
  "dom_id": "question-168604",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)=x{y}^{3}-x+y$ inside the square defined in part 4.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}_{\\text{ave}}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The interior of the square defined in the previous part can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\,:\\,-4<x<4,\\,-4<y<4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(R)=8\\cdot 8=64.\n$$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(R)}\\,{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}{\u222c}_{R}(x{y}^{3}-x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}(x{y}^{3}-x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}-xy+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=-4}^{y=4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}[(64x-4x+8)-(64x+4x+8)]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}(-8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{-4}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(16-16) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
